<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa money mkt shortage rises to 9.65 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.Africa money mkt shortage rises to 9.65 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank said the South African money market shortage rose to 9.650 billion rand on Wednesday from 9.132 billion rand on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Three-month NCD rates were quoted slightly higher at between 17.20 and 17.35 percent offered from 17.20 to 17.25 percent, while the 90-day BA rate also moved higher to between 16.65 and 16.95 percent from 16.55 and 16.90 percent previously.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
